# enc-frx runtime dependencies.
#
# Pulled from the Fractalyze package index alongside upstream PyPI:
#   pip install -r requirements.in \
#     --extra-index-url https://fractalyze.github.io/pypi/simple/
#
# hash-frx — the symmetric layer ML-KEM's sampling and hashing run through — is
# absent on purpose: it is a Bazel module, pinned by commit in //MODULE.bazel,
# not a wheel.
#
# The frx build is pinned to the one hash-frx pins, and the two must move
# together: hash-frx resolves frx from its own lock, so skew puts two different
# frx copies on one test's sys.path.
#
# zk_dtypes arrives via frx but is pinned here directly, because this repo has a
# floor of its own on it. AES and GCM are defined over binary fields this stack
# carries natively — `binary_field_gf8_aes` (GF(2^8), AES's reduction polynomial)
# and `binary_field_ghash` (GF(2^128), GCM's) — and those dtypes register in the
# frx frontend from zk_dtypes >= 0.0.10. Taken transitively, a frx bump could
# drop the thing AES-GCM is built on without anything here saying so.
absl-py
numpy
